  "id": "media-psychology",
  "term": "media psychology",
  "definition": "Media psychology is a psychological perspective for understanding how features of media experiences, such as emotional cues, story and task structure, ease of interaction, and clear links between actions and outcomes, influence involvement and intention. In this view, immersion can support engagement, but it is not the only factor shaping intentions.",
